# Created by https://www.toptal.com/developers/gitignore/

### Bazel ###
# gitignore template for Bazel build system
# website: https://bazel.build/

# Ignore all bazel-* symlinks. There is no full list since this can change
# based on the name of the directory bazel is cloned into.
/bazel-*

# Local Bazel settings (API keys, personal preferences)
user.bazelrc

# Directories for the Bazel IntelliJ plugin containing the generated
# IntelliJ project files and plugin configuration. Seperate directories are
# for the IntelliJ, Android Studio and CLion versions of the plugin.
/.ijwb/
/.aswb/
/.clwb/

### Rust ###
# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug/
target/

# Remove Cargo.lock from gitignore if creating an executable, leave it for libraries
# More information here https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html
# Cargo.lock also shall be removed from gitignore within Bazel enabled projects.
# Cargo.lock

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

### Go ###

# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#

# Enable go.mod explicitly as it conflicts with C++ Fortran exclusions
!go.mod

# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool, specifically when used with LiteIDE
*.out

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
